      "math_academy_id": "q-355398",
      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "Let $c(n)$ be a cost for option $n,$ where $n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}.$ We want to write the optimal option $\\overset{^}{n}$ as \"the value of $n$ that makes $c(n)$ as small as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $\\overset{^}{n}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We want $\\overset{^}{n}$ to be an *input value* $n$ where the cost $c(n)$ is as small as possible. \n\nThat is exactly what $\\operatorname{arg}⁡min$ returns.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{n}=\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{n\\in \\{3,5,7,9\\}}c(n).\n$$",
